.TH UAVLINK 1 "October 2026" "uavlink 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
uavlink \- set up the MAVLink link of a CM5 companion computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uavlink
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B uavlink
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uavlink
configures the MAVLink link between a Raspberry Pi CM5 companion computer, its flight controller (X25) and a ground
station or VPS: the router
.RB ( uavlink\-router.service ),
network, firewall, SSH and time settings, and the flight controller parameters.
.PP
Installing the package changes nothing. Changes are made by
.B apply
(or the setup page) from a preset plus your values, are recorded, and are undone by
.BR uninstall .
Commands that change the system need root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBsetup\fR [\fB\-\-lan\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-foreground\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR]
Start the temporary setup server
.RB ( uavlink\-setup.service )
and print the address of the setup page, with its access token.
.B \-\-lan
listens on all interfaces instead of 127.0.0.1,
.B \-\-port
changes the port (default 8090),
.B \-\-foreground
runs the server in this process and
.B \-\-no\-browser
does not open a browser. The server stops after 30 minutes without requests.
.TP
\fBserve\fR [\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-idle\fR \fISECS\fR]
Run the setup server in the foreground; this is what
.B uavlink\-setup.service
runs.
.TP
\fBapply \-\-preset\fR \fIID\fR [\fB\-\-role cm5\fR|\fBvps\fR] [\fB\-\-set\fR \fIKEY\fB=\fIVALUE\fR]... [\fB\-\-preview\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-props\-off\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
Apply a preset to this machine.
.B \-\-set
overrides one value and can be repeated,
.B \-\-preview
shows what would change and writes nothing,
.B \-\-yes
does not ask for confirmation,
.B \-\-props\-off
states that the propellers are removed, which allows the flight controller to be configured.
.B \-\-json
prints the raw events, one per line, and
.B \-\-verbose
shows file diffs and engine output.
When the firewall or SSH settings change over an SSH session, they are rolled back automatically unless
.B uavlink confirm
is run from a new SSH session in time.
.TP
\fBpresets\fR [\fB\-\-role cm5\fR|\fBvps\fR]
List the presets.
.TP
\fBconfig show\fR
Print the saved configuration (secrets masked).
.TP
\fBconfig get\fR \fIKEY\fR
Print one saved value.
.TP
\fBconfig set\fR \fIKEY\fB=\fIVALUE\fR...
Change saved values; they take effect at the next
.BR apply .
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show the state of the uavlink services and the time of the last apply and the last verify.
.TP
\fBverify\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
Run the acceptance checks of the applied configuration.
.TP
\fBconfirm\fR
Confirm the firewall/SSH change and stop the rollback timer
.RB ( uavlink\-rollback.timer ).
.TP
\fBx25 backups\fR
List the backups of the flight controller parameters.
.TP
\fBx25 restore\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-props\-off\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
Write a parameter backup back to the flight controller.
.TP
\fBuninstall\fR [\fB\-\-preview\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
Undo every change made by
.BR apply .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure, including a failed check or a cancelled confirmation.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, unknown preset or invalid value.
.TP
.B 4
Refused: root is required, another job is running, or the machine is not safe to change (vehicle armed, WSL).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/uavlink/config.env
Saved configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/uavlink/secrets.env
Saved secrets, readable by root only.
.TP
.I /var/lib/uavlink/
Record of the changes (used by
.BR uninstall ),
logs and flight controller parameter backups.
.TP
.I /usr/share/uavlink/presets/
Presets.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo uavlink setup
sudo uavlink apply \-\-preset dgp\-current \-\-preview
sudo uavlink apply \-\-preset dgp\-current
sudo uavlink confirm
uavlink status
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ufw (8)
